proposed experimental methodology

The drafting method begins with a rough idea, then chatbot conversation is used as an iterative development environment. The model is used to expand, challenge, reorganise, and restate the idea across multiple passes. The author reads every iteration, retains control over scope and claims, and decided which outputs are kept, revised, rejected, or moved to future work. No unread model output is treated as finished authorial material. The workflow is therefore not prompt-to-paper automation, but human-supervised iterative drafting.

The method uses staged human oversight rather than full close reading at every pass. Early model outputs are skimmed for sanity, object preservation, and useful direction. Promising material is then selected, rejected, merged, or redirected. As a draft stabilises, human review becomes more detailed, culminating in full close reading, claim checking, and final authorial audit. The workflow is therefore not unattended generation. It is light-touch iterative drafting followed by increasingly strict human verification.

The final stage uses a voice-restoration model pass. A dedicated system_witch instance receives a personality pack and rewrites the near-final draft toward the author’s intended voice, while preserving claims, scope, citations, and structure. This stage is followed by proofread jeopardy: a deliberate final check for seeded substitution, object substitution, homophones, unintended smoothing, and voice loss.
